    {
        "command": "delay",
        "value": 2
    },
    {
        "text": "Lemuen spots the one she came to see."
    },
    {
        "text": "The golden-haired Sankta stands under a porch. She is praying, anxious; her breathing is rapid, and she trembles visibly..."
    },
    {
        "text": "Lemuen can feel herself overwhelmed by her counterpart's raging emotions."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "Matriarch?"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "\u2014"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "I overheard your conversation with Velliv, Cardinal Lemuen... pardon my inability to converse calmly at this time."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "What's in there?"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "A Sarkaz mother."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "She spent much time in the wilderness, and declined food for two days after she arrived... she is not in good shape. Our Nurturers are doing their best."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "She suffers from fear and anxiety. She does not want to give in to the pain, and continues her struggle to stay awake..."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "She is praying, awake, praying that her child will be born safely."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "All I can do is empathize and pray with her."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "You can empathize with a Sarkaz?"
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "Yes, Cardinal."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "As you worry for my outpouring of emotion. It is as clear as the innate empathy between you and I."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "'Empathy'..."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "A blessing that the Lord has bestowed upon me, perhaps, in place of my sight... or perhaps simply because this place was built by Laterano to welcome new life."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "Here our faith is strengthened and expanded. Here, there are no barriers, no limits."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "Putting it in that light, it is our own people who need this place the most."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "..."
    },
    {
        "command": "dialog"
    },
    {
        "text": "Sunlight shines through the stained glass, illuminating the empty and solemn hall."
    },
    {
        "text": "The massive statue stands with its palms together, looking down on the two tiny Sanktas beneath it."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "It's certainly a special place."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Lemuen",
        "text": "I've seen plenty of statues in all sorts of poses, holding a gun and ready to shoot. But it's the first time I've seen one like this, and it takes some getting used to."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "Compared to the so-called 'Lateran statues' that line the hills of Bol\u00edvar or the shores of Iberia, the statues seen in Laterano are the more incomprehensible, Cardinal."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "Paradise has shaped our faith, so peculiar that it has become somewhat distorted."
    },
    {
        "command": "name",
        "value": "Matriarch",
        "text": "The souls of the living praying for survival, as they traverse Catastrophe and suffering... such is the most basic face of faith."
    },
    {
        "command": "dialog"
    },
